se | $(TESTDIR)\n\t$(SET_DLL_PATH) && $(RUN_CASE_CMD) \"... main.exe < .../t3_empty_case > nul 2> .../t3_empty_case\" $(NO_INPUT) && $(CHECK_CMD) $(CONTAINS) ... && $(TOUCH) $@\n```\nWith CMake function:\n```\nadd_case(t3_cpp_empty_case t3_bbox_cpp \"\" t3_empty_case t3_empty_case 66 contains)\n```\nOne line, because the function encodes \"run, check exit code, compare contains\". Not magic — but the pattern is written once.\n\nFor claim 2 example: `add_library(common_cpp_shared SHARED ...)` → CMake derives \"SHARED\" → on Linux add -fPIC, on Windows build an import lib and expect dllexport/dllimport wiring. And `target_link_libraries(t3_bbox_cpp PRIVATE common_cpp_shared)` → CMake adds the import lib to the link line and, at runtime for tests, knows the dll location (that's how PATH env can be auto-computed). But the *macro* COMMON_API logic is still in your headers and your target_compile_definitions.\n\nAlso I might mention: the \"представление о проекте\" is real and it's the actual payoff — ctest knows the tests, IDE can display targets, etc. But frame it correctly: the model is what YOU declared, and tools can *query* it. That's the \"data not text\" point from before.\n\nShould I ask a clarifying question? The plan-mode reminder says ask when weighing tradeoffs. Here we're in a comprehension check — I should verify understanding and correct. Maybe end with a micro-question to check the corrected model. Or just correct and ask \"переформулируй одним предложением\". \n\nLet me keep it focused and not too long. Structure:\n\n- Claim 1: верно по духу, три поправки.\n- Claim 2: половина верна, что именно верно и что нет, правильная модель.\n\nThen a short comprehension-check question back at her.\n\nLet me write in Russian, concise but thorough. Use her t3 example. Mark [ФАКТ]/[МНЕНИЕ] where appropriate per the anti-sycophancy protocol? The protocol asks me to tag categories and confidence. I should do that lightly.\n\nLet me write.",
