onfirm the user is right (and praise appropriately — no, anti-sycophancy but here they're genuinely right; I should confirm with facts).\n2. Explain why: on MSVC, /fsanitize=address is a compile-time option; the runtime is linked automatically via compiler-emitted references; the Makefile proved it (link step was just /DEBUG and ASan worked). On Linux/GCC, the sanitizer runtime must be explicitly linked, hence -fsanitize=address at link.\n\nSo we should correct the skeleton: make the MSVC link options `$<$<CONFIG:Debug>:/DEBUG>` and keep /fsanitize=address only in compile options for MSVC. And on Linux keep both.\n\nLet me double check: MSVC link /DEBUG in release: /DEBUG /OPT:REF /OPT:ICF. That's fine.\n\nSo the corrected configure_target MSVC branch:\n```\ntarget_compile_options(${tgt} PRIVATE $<$<CONFIG:Debug>:/Zi /fsanitize=address> $<$<CONFIG:Release>:/Zi>)\ntarget_link_options(${tgt} PRIVATE $<$<CONFIG:Debug>:/DEBUG> $<$<CONFIG:Release>:/DEBUG /OPT:REF /OPT:ICF>)\n```\n\nWait — but /Zi on MSVC with CMake: actually CMake might already add /Zi for Debug? Let me reconsider. Hmm. Actually I want to verify whether CMake adds /Zi by default. Let me quickly fetch the MSVC ASan doc and maybe the CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_DEBUG default. Actually let me fetch MSVC ASan doc for the link question — that's the key factual point. And maybe confirm /RTC/ASan conflict.\n\nLet me do webfetch for the MSVC /fsanitize=address documentation.\n\nActually, the user is in plan mode and asked two conceptual questions. I should answer them. I can verify with a quick fetch. Let me do one fetch for MSVC ASan docs.\n\nLet me fetch: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/sanitizers/asan\n\nAnd maybe the /RTC note. Let me do it.\n\nActually, let me reconsider the /Od question: CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_DEBUG default for MSVC. Let me recall the exact defaults:\n- CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_DEBUG (MSVC): `/D_DEBUG /MDd /Ob0 /Od /RTC1`\n- CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_RELEASE (MSVC): `/MD /O2 /Ob2 /DNDEBUG`\n\nBut with CMP0091 NEW, /MDd and /MD are removed from these strings (they're added via runtime library abstraction). So flags_DEBUG becomes `/D_DEBUG /Ob0 /Od /RTC1`. So /Od and /O2 are in the defaults. Good.\n\nSo answer Q1: Yes — /Od (Debug) and /O2 (Release) come from CMake's default per-config flags; /MDd and /MD come from the MSVC runtime library abstraction (CMP0091, enabled by our minimum version). What we add ourselves: /Zi (pdb info — not in CMake defaults) and ASan.\n\nHmm wait, but there's subtlety: is /Zi in the default? I need to be careful. I believe CMake's MSVC Debug default flags DON'T include /Zi. Let me verify... Actually I recall that for the VS generator, /Zi IS in the Debug settings because the default project templates add it. But for the generic flags... Hmm.\n\nActually, I'm fairly confident: CMake MSVC defaults do NOT include /Zi in CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_DEBUG. The /Zi is often added per target or via CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_DEBUG by projects. So keeping /Zi explicit in our configure_target is correct and matches the Makefile requirement (pdb always).\n\nLet me verify the /RTC1 + ASan conflict and the link behavior via a web fetch to be accurate. Let me fetch the ASan MSVC docs.\n\nActually, let me be efficient with time. The user is asking two questions. The most important correction: Q2 user is right — remove /fsanitize=address from MSVC link options. Let me verify with a fetch of MSVC ASan docs to confirm \"no link flag needed on MSVC\" and \"/RTC conflict\".\n\nLet me fetch https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/sanitizers/asan (or /error). This is a legit programming help URL.\n\nI'll do the fetch, then answer.",
