          "text": "Let me answer both questions based on facts gathered.\n\nQ1: /Od and /O2, /MD /MDd — will CMake do these automatically?\n\nLet me think about what CMake does by default on MSVC:\n- CMAKE_MSVC_RUNTIME_LIBRARY default is `MultiThreaded$<$<CONFIG:Debug>:Debug>DLL` which produces `/MD` for Release and `/MDd` for Debug. This is controlled by policy CMP0091, which our cmake_minimum_required(3.22) sets to NEW. So YES, /MD and /MDd are automatic.\n- Optimization flags: CMake sets per-config default flags. For MSVC:\n  - CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_DEBUG default includes `/D_DEBUG /MDd /Ob0 /Od /RTC1` (something like that). Actually CMake's default for Debug on MSVC: `/D_DEBUG /MDd /Ob0 /Od /RTC1`. With CMP0091 NEW, `/MDd` removed from that string and handled by abstraction. So `/Od` is automatic for Debug.\n  - CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_RELEASE includes `/MD /O2 /Ob2 /DNDEBUG`. So `/O2` is automatic for Release.\n  - But wait — is /O2 default in release? Yes, CMake default Release flags for MSVC: `/MD /O2 /Ob2 /DNDEBUG`.\n\nSo the answer: YES, /Od, /O2, /MD, /MDd are all handled by CMake automatically from the build type. BUT there's a subtlety: CMake's Release also adds /DNDEBUG. And CMake's Debug default might include /RTC1 which conflicts with ASan (the docs say ASan isn't compatible with /RTC). Actually the doc says incompatible with edit-and-continue, incremental linking, and /RTC. The IDE section says for an existing project using /Od you might need to turn off /ZI (EditAndContinue), /RTC1, /INCREMENTAL.\n\nWait, important: CMake's default MSVC Debug flags include `/RTC1`. And ASan docs say ASan isn't compatible with `/RTC`. So we need to remove /RTC1 when enabling ASan. This is a real detail I flagged earlier as [ПРЕДПОЛОЖЕНИЕ, СРЕДНИЙ]. Now I have doc evidence: \"However, it isn't compatible with edit-and-continue, incremental linking, and /RTC.\" So we need to override CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_DEBUG to remove /RTC1, or set per-target flags.\n\nActually, since we set flags via target_compile_options with genex, the CMake default flags (CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_DEBUG) will STILL be added to every target. So /RTC1 from the default debug flags would be present alongside our /fsanitize=address. That's a conflict. So we need to modify CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_DEBUG to remove /RTC1, OR set CMAKE_MSVC_RUNTIME_LIBRARY and adjust.\n\nAlso note: /Zi is NOT in CMake default flags for MSVC I think. Actually CMake for Debug includes... hmm. Let me think. Default CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_DEBUG for MSVC: \"/D_DEBUG /MDd /Ob0 /Od /RTC1\". No /Zi. So we add /Zi ourselves via genex (already in skeleton). Good.\n\nAlso the doc mentions /ZI (Edit and Continue) is incompatible with ASan. CMake default doesn't set /ZI, only /Zi. Actually there's a variable CMAKE_MSVC_DEBUG_INFORMATION_FORMAT that VS CMake integration sets to EditAndContinue for Debug. But that's for the VS generator's CMake integration; for Ninja generator, the default debug info format is ProgramDatabase (/Zi)? Hmm. Actually CMake sets /Zi for MSVC automatically? Let me think. CMake for MSVC: the debug information format is controlled by CMAKE_MSVC_DEBUG_INFORMATION_FORMAT, default is \"ProgramDatabase\" which adds /Zi to Debug and RelWithDebInfo. Hmm, is that right? There's a variable introduced in CMake 3.25: CMAKE_MSVC_DEBUG_INFORMATION_FORMAT, default \"ProgramDatabase\". For Debug and RelWithDebInfo configs it adds /Zi. So /Zi might be automatic for Debug in modern CMake (3.25+). But we're at 3.30.5. So Debug gets /Zi automatically via ProgramDatabase. For Release, no /Zi by default (Release config doesn't get debug info by default). The course wants /Zi in Release too (pdb always). So we still add /Zi for Release ourselves. That's fine, harmless to also add for Debug (or redundant).\n\nActually this is getting complex. The key points to answer the user:\n\nQ1: Yes, /Od, /O2, /MD, /MDd are done by CMake automatically based on CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE + CMP0091. What we must add ourselves: ASan, /Zi for Release, warnings, 