MSVC. \n\nAlso ASan needs /Zi (debug info) for good call stacks — we have /Zi in compile. And the doc says ASan incompatible with incremental linking and /RTC. CMake release default doesn't set /INCREMENTAL (that's MSBuild default, not CMake). For Ninja, no incremental linking. Good.\n\nSo the corrected link flags for MSVC Debug: just `/DEBUG` (and maybe /INFERASANLIBS is default ON). For Release: `/DEBUG /OPT:REF /OPT:ICF`. No /fsanitize=address at link on MSVC.\n\nOn Linux: keep -fsanitize=address at link (GCC needs it). The Makefile already had that: Linux LINK_FLAGS = -fsanitize=address. MSVC LINK_FLAGS = /DEBUG only. Good, consistent with Makefile.\n\nSo the user caught a real bug in my skeleton. The MSVC Debug link line should be `/DEBUG` only, not `/DEBUG /fsanitize=address`. The compile line has /fsanitize=address which is correct.\n\nAlso note: on MSVC, ASan requires /Zi for symbolization — we add /Zi in compile Debug. Good.\n\nLet me also double-check: does ASan on MSVC require /MDd? The doc says \"The option works with static and dynamic CRTs (/MD, /MDd, /MT, /MTd)\". So /MDd fine.\n\nSo my answer:\n\nQ1: Yes, /Od /O2 /MD /MDd are automatic from CMake. Details: /MD & /MDd via CMAKE_MSVC_RUNTIME_LIBRARY (CMP0091), /Od & /O2 from per-config default flags. BUT two nuances discovered from docs:\n- CMake Debug default includes /RTC1, which is incompatible with ASan → we must strip it from Debug flags.\n- /Zi for Debug is auto (ProgramDatabase); /Zi for Release we add ourselves.\nSo the skeleton should adjust: set CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_DEBUG to remove /RTC1.\n\nActually, wait — I need to reconsider whether to set /Od /O2 ourselves. The user asks \"будет делаться за счёт CMake?\" Answer: yes, automatically, you don't write /Od /O2 /MD /MDd. That's the main answer. But we need to remove /RTC1 from debug.\n\nQ2: User is right. On Windows ASan libs are auto-linked (docs). /fsanitize=address is only a compiler option on MSVC; do NOT pass it to link. On Linux, GCC needs -fsanitize=address at link. So fix skeleton: MSVC link Debug → /DEBUG only. This matches the Makefile (MSVC LINK_FLAGS debug = /DEBUG only). So user's intuition confirmed with doc citation.\n\nI'm in plan mode. I should present findings and update the plan/skeleton accordingly. No edits to files. I can present the corrected snippet in the answer.\n\nLet me also reconsider: the compile options line for MSVC in skeleton: `$<$<CONFIG:Debug>:/Zi /fsanitize=address> $<$<CONFIG:Release>:/Zi>`. This adds /Zi for both. But CMake already adds /Zi for Debug (ProgramDatabase default in 3.25+). Duplicate /Zi is harmless. Keep. Actually, to keep it clean, maybe drop /Zi for Debug since it's automatic, but harmless either way. I'll note it.\n\nBut there's the /RTC1 issue: with the skeleton as-is, Debug would get CMake default /RTC1 + our /fsanitize=address → conflict. So the plan must address this. Options:\n1. Override CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_DEBUG (and C flags) to remove /RTC1.\n2. Since tools don't get ASan, they could keep /RTC1, but simpler to remove globally.\n\nI'll propose: set per-config flags explicitly for MSVC:\n```\nset(CMAKE_C_FLAGS_DEBUG \"/D_DEBUG /Ob0 /Od\")\nset(CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_DEBUG \"/D_DEBUG /Ob0 /Od\")\n```\nwith /MDd coming from runtime lib abstraction. And keep /Zi via default or add manually.\n\nHmm, but actually if we set CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS_DEBUG ourselves, we override CMake defaults. Fine. This is clean.\n\nAlternatively use CMAKE_MSVC_DEBUG_INFORMATION_FORMAT and CMAKE_MSVC_RUNTIME_LIBRARY. Keep simple.\n\nLet me present the answer concisely but complete, with doc citations. And update the plan: skeleton correction for link options (remove /fsanitize=address from MSVC link) and debug flags (remove /RTC1). Then ask to confirm and start.\n\nSince I'm in plan mode, I just present the corrected plan. Let me write it.",
