          "text": "The user asks: for `configure_target(common_c_static ON)` — will configure_target only trigger `cl` but not `link`, because we used `add_library` not `add_executable`?\n\nLet me think carefully. `configure_target` itself doesn't compile or link anything — it only sets properties/options on the target. The actual compilation and linking happen at build time (`cmake --build`). \n\nBut the question is about the target type: `add_library(common_c_static STATIC geometry.c)` creates a static library target. At build time, CMake will compile `geometry.c` to an object file (`cl /c`) and then archive it into `common_c_static.lib` via `lib` (MSVC's librarian). So it's `cl` (compile) + `lib` (archive), NOT `link`. \n\nActually wait — the user's mental model seems to be: configure_target contains the compile options AND link options. For a static library, the link options are irrelevant (static libs aren't linked). So when you call `configure_target(common_c_static ON)`:\n- `target_compile_options` applies → at build time `cl /c` compiles.\n- `target_link_options` applies to the target but for a STATIC library, link options have no effect at link time because static libraries aren't linked — they're archived with `lib`.\n\nSo yes: the user is basically right. For a static library target, only compilation happens (cl /c) and then archiving (lib), no linking (link). The link options set in configure_target are inert for a static library.\n\nBut there's a nuance: `configure_target` doesn't DO the compilation. It just records options. The compilation happens at `cmake --build` time. So saying \"из configure_target произойдёт только cl\" is slightly imprecise — configure_target itself produces nothing; it attaches options that will be used later when building. The build for a static library does: `cl /c` (compile to .obj) then `lib /OUT:...lib` (archive). No `link`.\n\nAlso, for a static library, ASan, /Zi etc. still apply at compile time (they're compile options), which is correct — the library objects get instrumented. The link options (/DEBUG) are just inert for static lib.\n\nLet me also note: in our configure_target, the link options are inside `if(DBG)` — for common_c_static ON means DBG=ON so link options are set too, but they have no effect on a static library.\n\nSo answer: yes, essentially correct, with the refinement that configure_target itself compiles nothing — it just records flags. At build time, static library = compile (cl /c) + archive (lib), no link (link). The link options set on a static library are inert.\n\nKeep it concise. This is plan mode, just answering a comprehension question. No tools needed.",
