h Russian — but other CP1251 files also displayed with mojibake (like geometry.hpp). Wait no — geometry.hpp showed garbled characters (mojibake) because it's CP1251. But CMakeLists.txt shows proper Russian. So CMakeLists.txt is indeed UTF-8 (or the read tool decoded it correctly). Good — confirms UTF-8.\n\n**Issue 4: `configure_target` with DBG param — in `common/CMakeLists.txt` called with `ON`.** For static libraries, link options are inert (fine). Compile options apply. OK.\n\n**Issue 5: The `if(DBG)` for Linux tools — `else()` branch adds `-O2` for Release only.** That's agreed. Fine.\n\n**Issue 6: Potential problem — `configure_target` function must be defined BEFORE `add_subdirectory(common)` because common/CMakeLists.txt calls it.** In the root file, `configure_target` is defined at line 43, and `add_subdirectory(common)` at line 92. Good, defined before. ✓\n\n**Issue 7: `add_task` is defined but the common libs get `configure_target(... ON)`.** Since add_task also calls configure_target(ON), tasks get product flags. Good.\n\nBut again — **no add_task invocations exist**. This is the critical missing piece. Maybe the user hasn't added them yet (they're writing files incrementally and asked for review). I should point it out clearly.\n\n**Issue 8: Comment says \"имя проекта сохранится в CMAKE_PROJECT_NAME\"** — Actually `PROJECT_NAME` (not CMAKE_PROJECT_NAME). CMAKE_PROJECT_NAME is the name of the top-level project (also exists). Actually `CMAKE_PROJECT_NAME` is a real variable — \"Name of the project given to the top-level project() command\". And `PROJECT_NAME` is \"Name of the project given to the most recent project() command\". So the comment is slightly imprecise but both exist. Minor.\n\n**Issue 9: Line 42 comment \"важно следить за этим\"** — fine.\n\n**Issue 10: In `configure_target`, `$<$<CONFIG:Debug>:/Zi /fsanitize=address> $<$<CONFIG:Release>:/Zi>`** — on MSVC Debug, /Zi is added via genex AND CMake default Debug flags may already include /Zi? Act