parameter is `trgt`, and she also has a variable named `trgt`? No, it's fine.\n\nLet me also verify the encoding question: \"CMake-вещи тоже в utf-8, я верно помню?\" — Yes, that was the decision. Files are UTF-8 with BOM (EF BB BF). CMake reads UTF-8 fine. BOM is acceptable (CMake handles it). But note: the .editorconfig only specifies charset for .md. Could add CMakeLists.txt to editorconfig, but that's a minor suggestion.\n\nActually, wait — one thing about the BOM. Is it a problem? CMake supports UTF-8 BOM in CMakeLists.txt. clang-format doesn't touch CMakeLists. So fine. I'll mention it's UTF-8 with BOM, which is fine.\n\nNow the commands reminder:\n```\ncmake -B build/cmake-debug -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug\ncmake --build build/cmake-debug\n```\nWait — why `build/cmake-debug`? Earlier I proposed a separate directory `build/cmake-debug` to avoid clobbering make's `build/debug`. Hmm, actually in the plan I said build/cmake-debug for the transition period so CMake doesn't overwrite make's artifacts (parity check needs both). Let me recall: \"Почему отдельный каталог build/cmake-debug: чтобы CMake не затёр артефакты make-сборки\". Yes, for the parity check we need make artifacts in build/debug and cmake artifacts in build/cmake-debug to compare. So:\n\n```\ncmake -B build/cmake-debug -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug\ncmake --build build/cmake-debug\n```\nAnd make: `make t1_cpp t1_c` (or make all).\n\nThen parity check using run_case and check from make's build.\n\nLet me also note: since we pass -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug explicitly, the default in CMakeLists (if NOT CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE) won't trigger. That's fine — we pass it explicitly for parity testing. Actually the default is a fallback; explicitly passing Debug is fine and matches what I told her.\n\nAlso the release command:\n```\ncmake -B build/cmake-release -G Ninja -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Release\n```\nBut we're on Debug stage, so just note it.\n\nLet me formulate the review results clearly:\n\n**Errors found:**\n\n1. CRITICAL: No `add_task` invocations in root CMakeLists.txt. The function is defined but never called → no executables will be built. Add after line 92:\n```cmake\nadd_task(t1_dist_matrix_cpp t1_cpp t1_dist_matrix_cpp/main.cpp common_cpp_static)\nadd_task(t1_dist_matrix_c   t1_c   t1_dist_matrix_c/main.c     common_c_static)\n```\n\nEverything else checks out. Let me list the verified-correct items briefly and flag minor comments.\n\nAlso there's a small note: comment at line 42 \"полагается на слова deepseek-a\" — personal note, fine but will be awkward on контрольная точка (mentor sees it). Not an error.\n\nActually let me reconsider — is there anything about `add_subdirectory(common)` vs function visibility... `configure_target` is defined before add_subdirectory, so visible. ✓\n\nAlso: does `common/CMakeLists.txt` need `configure_target`? The function references `MSVC` variable and `DBG` param. Fine.\n\nOne more consideration — the tools (run_case/check) in tests/ aren't part of this CMake yet. The parity check for t1 only uses exit codes, which need run_case. But run_case is built by make (in build/debug/tools/). For commit 1 parity, we can use the make-built run_case against both make-built and cmake-built exes. That's fine and was the plan.\n\nLet me write the response in Russian, concise, structured. This is plan mode — I present findings, no edits. The user asked to \"check\" and \"remind\" — I should report findings and remind commands, and since add_task is missing, note it as the one fix needed (which will be done in execution phase).\n\nLet me be careful about the BOM: EF BB BF = UTF-8 BOM. Both files have it presumably. Actually only checked root. Fine.\n\nLet me write.",
