          "text": "The user asks: \"то есть ninja - аналог make, с другим синтаксисом и обновляет и по содержимому, и по времени?\"\n\nShe's asking to confirm: ninja is an analog of make, with different syntax, and it updates both by content and by time?\n\nLet me answer this precisely. Ninja IS the analog of make (both are build systems / сборщики). But the \"по содержимому\" part needs nuance. Let me think carefully.\n\nmake: decides rebuild based on timestamps only. If prereq is newer than target → rebuild.\n\nninja: primarily uses timestamps too, BUT:\n1. It stores the command used to build each output in .ninja_log (and .ninja_deps). If the command changed, it rebuilds even if timestamps are fine. So \"по содержимому\" — actually it's \"по команде/правилу\", not exactly by content. It compares the recorded command with the current command.\n2. It uses depfiles (.d files) from the compiler to know header dependencies — so it rebuilds when headers change, which make doesn't know unless you tell it. So in a sense it \"sees more\" — dependencies come from compiler, not hand-written.\n\nSo the correction: ninja doesn't compare file *contents* — it compares:\n- timestamps (like make),\n- AND the command line recorded vs current (rule changed → rebuild),\n- AND header deps from depfiles (rebuilds on header change, which make misses without manual dep lists).\n\nSo \"обновляет и по содержимому\" — not exactly by content; it's by recorded command. And the file comparison isn't content-hash. But the effect: it catches changes make misses. Let me be precise.\n\nAlso should I verify the exact claim about ninja comparing command? This is documented behavior. Ninja's .ninja_log stores the command hash per output. When the build.ninja is regenerated with a different command, ninja rebuilds because the command differs. Yes.\n\nLet me keep the answer concise and precise, in Russian, mark categories/confidence per the anti-sycophancy protocol. And confirm the plan still stands. 