\nActually, running `cmake --build --help` is read-only, no system change. Let me do it to be accurate.\n\nAlso the analogy to `make all`: yes, `cmake --build <dir>` with no `--target` builds the default target (ALL), which in our project is `all` → builds all tasks. So \"очень условно — да, аналог make all\".\n\nAlso note: ninja is parallel by default (uses all cores), whereas make defaults to serial. So -j8 is less critical with ninja. But with make-based generator (e.g., Unix Makefiles on Linux), -j matters.\n\nLet me run the help command to verify exact options.",
