e it's from CMake's default flags. Actually, I'm fairly confident: CMake's MSVC default flags DO NOT include /FS; but for the Ninja generator, CMake sets `/FS` in the default CMAKE_<LANG>_FLAGS when `MSVC` and Ninja because Ninja is parallel. Hmm, I'm not 100% sure of the exact mechanism. I could check CMakeCache or the compiler flags file. Let me not overclaim — I'll say it's added by CMake (it's not in our CMakeLists), likely because Ninja builds in parallel, and its purpose is to serialize PDB writes to prevent conflicts. I can verify by grepping the cache for where flags come from. Actually, let me quickly check the CMakeCache / CMakeCCompiler.cmake to see the flags, read-only.\n\nActually, let me check the build.ninja or the compiler flags file to confirm /FS source. build.ninja is 161 bytes — tiny, probably just includes rules.ninja. Let me check CMakeCCompiler.cmake and rules.ninja.\n\nActually, I can grep for /FS in the CMakeFiles to see where it comes from. Let me do a quick read-only grep.\n\nLet me also reconsider: is there anything about /FS conflicting with ASan? No — /FS is about PDB writes, unrelated to ASan. And /FS does NOT cause the LNK4099 they saw; that was the PDB timing with shared vc140.pdb in make. With per-target /Fd, /FS is harmless.\n\nLet me grep for where /FS comes from.",
