            "output": "  cmake-generators(7) — CMake 4.4.3 Documentation          \n\n### Navigation\n\n-   [index](../genindex.html \"General Index\")\n-   [next](../generator/Borland%20Makefiles.html \"Borland Makefiles\") |\n-   [previous](cmake-generator-expressions.7.html \"cmake-generator-expressions(7)\") |\n\n-   ![](../_static/cmake-logo-16.png) [CMake](https://cmake.org/) 4.4.3 »\n-   [Documentation](../index.html) »\n-   cmake-generators(7)\n\n# [cmake-generators(7)](#id7)[¶](#cmake-generators-7 \"Link to this heading\")\n\nContents\n\n-   [cmake-generators(7)](#cmake-generators-7)\n    \n    -   [Introduction](#introduction)\n        \n    -   [CMake Generators](#cmake-generators)\n        \n        -   [Command-Line Build Tool Generators](#command-line-build-tool-generators)\n            \n            -   [Makefile Generators](#makefile-generators)\n                \n            -   [Ninja Generators](#ninja-generators)\n                \n            -   [FASTBuild Generator](#fastbuild-generator)\n                \n        -   [IDE Build Tool Generators](#ide-build-tool-generators)\n            \n            -   [Visual Studio Generators](#visual-studio-generators)\n                \n            -   [Other Generators](#other-generators)\n                \n    -   [Extra Generators](#extra-generators)\n        \n\n## [Introduction](#id8)[¶](#introduction \"Link to this heading\")\n\nA *CMake Generator* is responsible for writing the input files for a native build system. Exactly one of the [CMake Generators](#cmake-generators) must be selected for a build tree to determine what native build system is to be used. Optionally one of the [Extra Generators](#extra-generators) may be selected as a variant of some of the [Command-Line Build Tool Generators](#command-line-build-tool-generators) to produce project files for an auxiliary IDE.\n\nCMake Generators are platform-specific so each may be available only on certain platforms. The [`cmake(1)`](cmake.1.html#manual:cmake\\(1\\) \"cmake(1)\") command-line tool [`--help`](cmake.1.html#cmdoption-cmake-h) output lists available generators on the current platform. Use its [`-G`](cmake.1.html#cmdoption-cmake-G) option to specify the generator for a new build tree. The [`cmake-gui(1)`](cmake-gui.1.html#manual:cmake-gui\\(1\\) \"cmake-gui(1)\") offers interactive selection of a generator when creating a new build tree.\n\n## [CMake Generators](#id9)[¶](#cmake-generators \"Link to this heading\")\n\n### [Command-Line Build Tool Generators](#id10)[¶](#command-line-build-tool-generators \"Link to this heading\")\n\nThese generators support command-line build tools. In order to use them, one must launch CMake from a command-line prompt whose environment is already configured for the chosen compiler and build tool.\n\n#### [Makefile Generators](#id11)[¶](#makefile-generators \"Link to this heading\")\n\n-   [Borland Makefiles](../generator/Borland%20Makefiles.html)\n-   [MSYS Makefiles](../generator/MSYS%20Makefiles.html)\n-   [MinGW Makefiles](../generator/MinGW%20Makefiles.html)\n-   [NMake Makefiles](../generator/NMake%20Makefiles.html)\n-   [NMake Makefiles JOM](../generator/NMake%20Makefiles%20JOM.html)\n-   [Unix Makefiles](../generator/Unix%20Makefiles.html)\n-   [Watcom WMake](../generator/Watcom%20WMake.html)\n\n#### [Ninja Generators](#id12)[¶](#ninja-generators \"Link to this heading\")\n\n-   [Ninja](../generator/Ninja.html)\n-   [Ninja Multi-Config](../generator/Ninja%20Multi-Config.html)\n\n#### [FASTBuild Generator](#id13)[¶](#fastbuild-generator \"Link to this heading\")\n\n-   [FASTBuild](../generator/FASTBuild.html)\n\n### [IDE Build Tool Generators](#id14)[¶](#ide-build-tool-generators \"Link to this heading\")\n\nThese generators support Integrated Development Environment (IDE) project files. Since the IDEs configure their own environment one may launch CMake from any environment.\n\n#### [Visual Studio Generators](#id15)[¶](#visual-studio-generators \"Link to this heading\")\n\n-   [Visual Studio 6](../generator/Visual%20Studio%206.html)\n-   [Visual Studio 7](../generator/Visual%20Studio%207.html)\n-   [Visual Studio 7 .NET 2003](../generator/Visual%20Studio%207%20.NET%202003.html)\n-   [Visual Studio 8 2005](../generator/Visual%20Studio%208%202005.html)\n-   [Visual Studio 9 2008](../generator/Visual%20Studio%209%202008.html)\n-   [Visual Studio 10 2010](../generator/Visual%20Studio%2010%202010.html)\n-   [Visual Studio 11 2012](../generator/Visual%20Studio%2011%202012.html)\n-   [Visual Studio 12 2013](../generator/Visual%20Studio%2012%202013.html)\n-   [Visual Studio 14 2015](../generator/Visual%20Studio%2014%202015.html)\n-   [Visual Studio 15 2017](../generator/Visual%20Studio%2015%202017.html)\n-   [Visual Studio 16 2019](../generator/Visual%20Studio%2016%202019.html)\n-   [Visual Studio 17 2022](../generator/Visual%20Studio%2017%202022.html)\n-   [Visual Studio 18 2026](../generator/Visual%20Studio%2018%202026.html)\n\n#### [Other Generators](#id16)[¶](#other-generators \"Link to this heading\")\n\n-   [Green Hills MULTI](../generator/Green%20Hills%20MULTI.html)\n-   [Xcode](../generator/Xcode.html)\n\n## [Extra Generators](#id17)[¶](#extra-generators \"Link to this heading\")\n\nDeprecated since version 3.27: Support for \"Extra Generators\" is deprecated and will be removed from a future version of CMake. IDEs may use the [`cmake-file-api(7)`](cmake-file-api.7.html#manual:cmake-file-api\\(7\\) \"cmake-file-api(7)\") to view CMake-generated project build trees.\n\nSome of the [CMake Generators](#cmake-generators) listed in the [`cmake(1)`](cmake.1.html#manual:cmake\\(1\\) \"cmake(1)\") command-line tool [`--help`](cmake.1.html#cmdoption-cmake-h) output may have variants that specify an extra generator for an auxiliary IDE tool. Such generator names have the form `<extra-generator> - <main-generator>`. The following extra generators are known to CMake.\n\n-   [CodeBlocks](../generator/CodeBlocks.html)\n-   [CodeLite](../generator/CodeLite.html)\n-   [Eclipse CDT4](../generator/Eclipse%20CDT4.html)\n-   [Kate](../generator/Kate.html)\n-   [Sublime Text 2](../generator/Sublime%20Text%202.html)\n\n### Table of Contents\n\n-   [cmake-generators(7)](#)\n    -   [Introduction](#introduction)\n    -   [CMake Generators](#cmake-generators)\n        -   [Command-Line Build Tool Generators](#command-line-build-tool-generators)\n            -   [Makefile Generators](#makefile-generators)\n            -   [Ninja Generators](#ninja-generators)\n            -   [FASTBuild Generator](#fastbuild-generator)\n        -   [IDE Build Tool Generators](#ide-build-tool-generators)\n            -   [Visual Studio Generators](#visual-studio-generators)\n            -   [Other Generators](#other-generators)\n    -   [Extra Generators](#extra-generators)\n\n#### Previous topic\n\n[cmake-generator-expressions(7)](cmake-generator-expressions.7.html \"previous chapter\")\n\n#### Next topic\n\n[Borland Makefiles](../generator/Borland%20Makefiles.html \"next chapter\")\n\n### This Page\n\n-   [Show Source](../_sources/manual/cmake-generators.7.rst.txt)\n\n### Quick search \n\n### Navigation\n\n-   [index](../genindex.html \"General Index\")\n-   [next](../generator/Borland%20Makefiles.html \"Borland Makefiles\") |\n-   [previous](cmake-generator-expressions.7.html \"cmake-generator-expressions(7)\") |\n\n-   ![](../_static/cmake-logo-16.png) [CMake](https://cmake.org/) 4.4.3 »\n-   [Documentation](../index.html) »\n-   cmake-generators(7)\n\n© Copyright 2000-2026 Kitware, Inc. and Contributors. Created using [Sphinx](https://www.sphinx-doc.org/) 8.2.3.",
